---
// HIDDEN until the season-sim check passes (config site.title_odds). To restore: move back to src/pages/
// and re-add the nav entry in layouts/Base.astro.
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import DotCompare from "../components/DotCompare.astro";
import { load, pct, TEAM } from "../lib/data";
const t = load<any>("title_odds.json", { rows: [] });
const rows = [...t.rows].sort((a: any, b: any) => Math.max(b.model, b.polymarket ?? 0) - Math.max(a.model, a.polymarket ?? 0));
const top = rows.slice(0, 16);
const gap = (r: any) => Math.abs(r.model - (r.polymarket ?? r.model));
const why = [...t.rows].sort((a: any, b: any) => gap(b) - gap(a)).slice(0, 6);
---
<Base title="Title odds" active="title-odds">
  <h1>2027 championship odds</h1>
  <p class="lede">The model plays out the whole season 50,000 times — every scheduled game, the play-in and four playoff
    rounds — and counts how often each team wins the title. Polymarket's champion market is shown alongside.</p>
  <DotCompare rows={top.map((r: any) => ({ label: r.team, a: r.model, b: r.polymarket }))}
    aLabel="Model" bLabel="Polymarket" aColor="var(--s-model)" bColor="var(--s-poly)" />
  <h2>Where the model and the market disagree</h2>
  <p class="small">The gaps are large, and the market is the better-informed side until proven otherwise. The simulation
    uses exactly the team strengths behind the daily game forecasts: a team rating from results (last season's, shrunk
    25% toward average over the summer) plus the expected strength of the current roster from player ratings. Most of the
    disagreement comes from the second part. Teams whose rosters rate well on last season's player data — Denver, Houston —
    climb far above their team rating; last season's champion, New York, does not.</p>
  <div class="table-scroll card"><table class="small">
    <thead><tr><th>Team</th><th>Team rating (rank)</th><th>Roster vs league avg.</th><th>Combined (rank)</th>
      <th>Model: champion</th><th>Polymarket</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{why.map((r: any) => <tr><td>{TEAM[r.team] ?? r.team}</td><td>{r.elo.toFixed(0)} ({r.rank_elo})</td>
      <td>{r.avail_rel > 0 ? "+" : "−"}{Math.abs(r.avail_rel).toFixed(0)}</td><td>{r.strength.toFixed(0)} ({r.rank_strength})</td>
      <td>{pct(r.model, 1)}</td><td>{pct(r.polymarket, 1)}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
  <p class="small">What the model does not know: player aging and development, coaching changes, health beyond the official
    injury report, and playoff results — by design they do not move ratings. Preseason uncertainty is a ±65-point spread
    per team, measured from how far teams moved from their preseason rating in 2022-26. Rating points: 28 ≈ one point of
    margin per game.</p>
  <h2>All teams</h2>
  <div class="table-scroll card"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Team</th><th>Conf.</th><th>Avg. wins</th><th>Model: conf. title</th><th>Model: champion</th><th>Polymarket: champion</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{rows.map((r: any) => <tr><td>{TEAM[r.team] ?? r.team}</td><td>{r.conference}</td><td>{r.mean_wins.toFixed(1)}</td>
      <td>{pct(r.model_conf, 1)}</td><td>{pct(r.model, 1)}</td><td>{pct(r.polymarket, 1)}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p class="small muted">{t.note}{t.polymarket_at && ` Polymarket snapshot: ${new Date(t.polymarket_at).toUTCString()}.`}</p>
</Base>
